      "language": null,
      "description": "An attacker brute-forced a Moats team member's Hetzner hosting account and gained access to the backend server storing private keys for the protocol's automated-rewards administrator wallets. Using the compromised administrative privileges, the attacker withdrew rewards, staked assets and locked tokens from Moats with automated rewards enabled on Avalanche and Robinhood Chain, causing approximately $600K in losses. The smart contracts themselves were not exploited; the incident originated from compromised hosting infrastructure and privileged keys stored on the server"
